&#x201C; Paper Tiger &#x201D; director James Gray has launched six of his nine feature films from the starry heights of the Cannes Film Festival , most recently contending for the Palme d&#x2019;Or this year with his New York-set crime drama.

Just don&#x2019;t expect to see him back on the Croisette anytime soon.

&#x201C;Cannes sucks. Don&#x2019;t worry, I'm not going back to Cannes,&#x201D; the director quipped Tuesday at the Marrakech Film Festival . &#x201C;I&#x2019;ve learned my lesson. Cannes is not for me. I am not for Cannes.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Anthony Mackie and Jamie Dornan’s Heist Drama '12 12 12' Feels Like a Bad Video Game: TV Review

Appearing in conversation with Venice Film Festival director Alberto Barbera, the Queens-born filmmaker was speaking to a full house that included &#x201C;Artificial&#x201D; director Luca Guadagnino and screen icon and Marrakech tribute award recipient Jeff Goldblum.

Over the course of 90 freewheeling minutes, Gray delighted the audience with tales from his New York upbringing, opening up about his tussles with the Hollywood studios that refused to release his movies and offering his take on the often chilly critical responses to many of his films &#x2014; beginning with his audacious debut &#x201C;Little Odessa,&#x201D; which won a Silver Lion in Venice in 1994, when the director was just 25 years old.

"That&#x2019;s the history of movies. It takes 10 years for you to understand if it&#x2019;s anything at all. Right, Luca? Isn&#x2019;t that true? Nobody knows anything," he said. "They really don&#x2019;t know what the fuck they&#x2019;re talking about."

At the tail end of an audience Q&A, Gray was asked about the role that festival competitions play in the movie industry today. Though his tongue was partly planted in cheek as he trashed the prestigious French fest &#x2014; where he's never won an award &#x2014; the director didn&#x2019;t mince words as he ripped into the "idiotic" concept of pitting movies against each other. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;I think the idea of the competition is terrible. I took the films [to Cannes] because the distributor wants it. They want that dumb logo on the film, but the idea is really dumb. We know that it&#x2019;s dumb,&#x201D; he said.

&#x201C;Euripides felt very bad because he wasn&#x2019;t winning a lot of prizes. It&#x2019;s true, by the way. He wound up living his life in a cave out of shame for not winning the prizes,&#x201D; Gray continued. &#x201C;I don&#x2019;t know who won the prizes during Euripides&#x2019; time. But the point is that I don&#x2019;t know who won the prizes. The whole thing is idiotic. It&#x2019;s not sports, you know?&#x201D;

The director was just warming up, directing his ire at the corporations that &#x201C;have done an excellent job at restricting access to a free flow of information and art.&#x201D;

&#x201C;What has the corporation done for us? 'You, shoot your movie in Atlanta. Shoot your movie in Budapest. Edit your movie in London.' Why? &#x2018;It&#x2019;s cheaper,&#x2019;&#x201D; said Gray. &#x201C;Not just because it's cheaper. Clusters of talent mean risk. Clusters of talent mean artists can gang up. Clusters of talent mean the New Hollywood, when a bunch of hippies ran the show, and they didn&#x2019;t like that at all. A cluster of talent means Fellini, Visconti, De Sica, Rossellini &#x2014; all those people working together. And the corporation doesn&#x2019;t like it. That&#x2019;s risk.&#x201D;

The director went on, saying, &#x201C;So what does the festival do? Communality. A bunch of filmmakers get together." He gestured to his pal Guadagnino, seated front and center in the audience. &#x201C;I see Luca. He&#x2019;s here in Marrakech. I can have dinner with him. He doesn&#x2019;t want to have dinner with me, maybe. But the point is that that communality is critical.

&#x201C;What is the thing in festivals that matters to the corporation? The competition. What wins. Why? That&#x2019;s the thing that&#x2019;s going to make them money,&#x201D; he continued. &#x201C;I hate the part where you compete. It&#x2019;s dumb; ethically, morally bankrupt. But it&#x2019;s also aiding and abetting the machine.&#x201D;

Instead, Gray celebrated film festivals as a space for &#x201C;the free-flowing exchange of ideas of thoughts" and championed them "as a communal thing, where we compare ideas and fight over films."

"&#x2018;I like that one. I hate that one.&#x2019; That's the coin of the realm. That is everything, and that's beautiful,&#x201D; he said. &#x201C;So anything that encourages a clustering of ideas, of thoughts, comparing and contrasting ideas: That is how we grow. To teach is also to learn. I think festivals are vitally important for that reason.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Fresh off an appearance at the Doha Film Festival , where &#x201C;Paper Tiger&#x201D; had its regional premiere, Gray has been making the rounds with his crime drama, which follows two brothers whose pursuit of the American Dream draws them into a dangerous scheme involving the Russian mafia. Starring Adam Driver, Miles Teller and Scarlett Johansson, the director&#x2019;s ninth feature was released theatrically by Neon earlier this month.

Gray is among the star-studded lineup participating in the Conversations series in Marrakech. Other A-listers appearing this week include screen stars John Turturro and Goldblum &#x2014; both recipients of tribute awards at the festival &#x2014; &#x201C;Knives Out&#x201D; director Rian Johnson, &#x201C;Artificial&#x201D; director Guadagnino and Italian screen icon Monica Bellucci.

The Marrakech Film Festival runs Nov. 20 &#x2013; 28.

James Marsden dominated social media buzz after Disney and Marvel Studios launched the final "Avengers: Doomsday" trailer , which ended on the viral moment of Marsden's Cyclops uniting the X-Men and Avengers in battle against Robert Downey Jr.'s Doctor Doom. Marsden event got to recite his character's iconic line: "To me, my X-Men!" Whether or not Marvel should've spoiled such a huge moment in the "Doomsday" trailer is now being widely debated among Marvel fans, but for Marsden it was moments like these that lured him back to playing Cyclops after 20 years. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Anthony Mackie and Jamie Dornan’s Heist Drama '12 12 12' Feels Like a Bad Video Game: TV Review

"One of the things people have said for years is that Cyclops is a leader, yet in many of the previous films he often took a back seat to Wolverine and some of the other characters," Marsden told Sharp magazine in a profile that published the same day as the "Doomsday" final trailer launch.

"There are only so many minutes available in a film this large, but it was important to me that my return felt meaningful," he continued. "I didn&#x2019;t want Cyclops to simply appear for a nostalgic cameo and then disappear. I wanted there to be a genuine purpose behind his presence. Without giving anything away, I feel very good about what we were able to do with the character.&#x201D;

Marsden debuted as Scott Summers/Cyclops in 2000&#x2019;s &#x201C;X-Men&#x201D; and reprised the role in 2003&#x2019;s &#x201C;X2: X-Men United&#x201D; and 2006&#x2019;s &#x201C;X-Men: The Last Stand.&#x201D; The character was killed off in the latter film, as Marsden moved on to film &#x201C;Superman Returns.&#x201D; But now Cyclops is back for &#x201C;Doomsday&#x201D; and leading the X-Men crew, which includes his original co-stars such as Patrick Stewart (Charles Xavier), Ian McKellen (Magneto), Kelsey Grammer (Beast), Alan Cumming (Nightcrawler) and Rebecca Romijn (Mystique). blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Why did " Avengers: Doomsday " narrow in on these X-Men and not others such as Halle Berry&#x2019;s Storm or Anna Paquin&#x2019;s Rogue? Co-director Joe Russo recently told Entertainment Weekly the casting decisions were "really targeted. It was really specific."

&#x201C;We really do have a process where we see the entire film through each character&#x2019;s eyes, no matter what the size of their role is,&#x201D; Anthony Russo added.. &#x201C;With the X-Men, we got to really deep dive and think about their histories as characters, their experiences, and how this particular moment in time was gonna affect them. There&#x2019;s such a rich history to them that we really do bring them to the film as if it&#x2019;s their movie, as well.&#x201D;

"Avengers: Doomsday" opens in theaters Dec. 18.

The horror satire &#x201C; Namaslay &#x201D; will be available to stream on Apple TV, Amazon, Fandango at Home and Google Pay on Dec. 15.

Directed by brothers Kanish Arhant-Sudhir and Rish Arhant-Sudhir, their feature film debut follows a grieving woman, Gayatri (Kirunthuja Srikanth-Talim), who is invited by her friend Judy (Angela Sant&#x2019;Albano) to an upscale yoga studio to to reconnect with the yoga traditions she inherited from her late grandmother. The result is a fiery conversation about the appropriation of yoga in the West, proving culture is the blood that keeps the past alive. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Anthony Mackie and Jamie Dornan’s Heist Drama '12 12 12' Feels Like a Bad Video Game: TV Review

&#x201C;We&#x2019;re thrilled to bring &#x2018;Namaslay&#x2019; to an even wider audience through its digital release,&#x201D; Rish and Kanish said in a statement. &#x201C;We made this film to be experienced, shared and talked about and we&#x2019;re excited that audiences across the country will have the opportunity to discover the world we created. As we continue our awards campaign, we&#x2019;re grateful to everyone who has supported the film and look forward to its next chapter with audiences wherever they watch.&#x201D;

To develop the meaningful story they wanted to share with audiences, the brothers turned inward to their real relationships and families&#x2019; lived experiences.

&#x201C;There&#x2019;s something that&#x2019;s truly slapstick almost about the whole experience, but then there&#x2019;s also something beneath that&#x2019;s kind of sinister,&#x201D; Rish said during the Variety Screening Series panel . &#x201C;It&#x2019;s a lot of strains of colonialism, there&#x2019;s commoditization that&#x2019;s happening, there is an extraction and then a resale at a premium.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Kanish echoed, &#x201C;An identity is not a story. It&#x2019;s a part of a character that affects how they interact with a story, and there are a lot of movies that have characters who have various identities that are not palpable at all, but the identity of a character in and of itself is not enough to undergird a narrative.&#x201D;

Alongside Srikanth-Talim and Sant&#x2019;Albano, &#x201C;Namaslay&#x201D; stars Alicia Mitchell-Mangual, Usha Krishnan and Christina Moore. The film is produced by Venk Potula via Khrisp Entertainment, alongside producers Rish and Kanish through their independent film studio Junghal Studios.

Andrew Scott remembers first learning about HIV and AIDS when he was growing up in Dublin, Ireland.

&#x201C;I would have been incredibly young, but I remember Oprah Winfrey talking about it,&#x201D; he tells me. &#x201C;She did quite a lot. She had Magic Johnson. That was a little bit later, but I remember she had Magic Johnson on her show and she spoke about the crisis. She had people who were living with HIV. It seemed kind of far away at the time.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories ‘PAW Patrol’ Spinoff Series ‘Skye’s Pup Squad’ Set for 2027 Release

Scott is now at the center of the conversation because of his starring role in &#x201C; Elsinore .&#x201D; He plays Ian Charleson , a star of the 1981 Oscar-winning &#x201C;Chariots of Fire,&#x201D; who starred in a 1989 production of &#x201C;Hamlet&#x201D; as he was dying of AIDS at the National Theatre in London.

Charleson never publicly revealed his sexuality or his illness before passing away just weeks after completing his run in &#x201C;Hamlet.&#x201D;

Scott came out in 2013 in an interview with &#x201C;The Independent.&#x201D;

&#x201C;I relate to it deeply, and I relate to it as a professional who wants to just do my job and as somebody who feels very grateful to get those opportunities that Ian and his counterparts didn&#x2019;t,&#x201D; says Scott, who is considered a front-runner in the Oscar race for best actor. &#x201C;I feel celebratory that I can look around and that there are out gay actors who are growing in number and not placing us in this insidious heaviness burden about separating actors in that way. It feels really wonderful that we have a lot of out gay actors in the movie in a movie about there not being a lot of out gay actors.&#x201D;

Director Simon Stone says casting an openly gay actor as Charleson was &#x201C;hugely important.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;I think what message that sends to the world is that times have changed, and that we&#x2019;re not going to apologize for the story that we&#x2019;re telling here,&#x201D; he says. &#x201C;Andrew has had the huge benefit of the pioneering work of so many actors before him, that his career was not disadvantaged at all by being openly gay. He&#x2019;s probably the first generation of actors who can say that.&#x201D;

&#x201C;Elsinore&#x201D; also stars Billie Piper as Patsy, Charleson&#x2019;s best friend who took care of him through his illness. Piper remembers Stone being mindful of how heavy that subject matter was. &#x201C;It was a very sensitive set. Simon was very good at setting a very peaceful environment,&#x201D; Piper says. &#x201C;People were in their socks, sort of padding around. It felt like a womb. It felt like a nest. People could be extremely emotional. I think a lot of the crew were very upset watching takes. I think for the actors sometimes you&#x2019;re so adrenalized that you&#x2019;re sort of just in it. Reflection is something that sometimes comes later.&#x201D;

The &#x201C;Elsinore&#x201D; cast also includes Olivia Colman as Charleson&#x2019;s physician, Dr. Margaret Johnson, David Dawson as filmmaker Derek Jarman and Joe Locke as a fellow AIDS patient.

Screenwriter Stephen Beresford&#x2019;s research included talking to the real &#x201C;fantastically generous&#x201D; Patsy as well as many other people who knew Charleson. &#x201C;Some of the people I spoke to are not in great health now, who are older,&#x201D; Beresford says. &#x201C;But they made the effort to come and talk to me because they wanted to honor Ian, and that&#x2019;s very special.&#x201D;

As Charleson&#x2019;s health deteriorates in the film, he develops Kaposi sarcoma lesions on his skin. Scott says he tried not to pay attention to the transfer tattoos that makeup department head Nadia Stacey applied to his skin to duplicate the dark cancerous growths.

&#x201C;In some ways, a little bit like Ian, I had to try and think, &#x2018;Well, they aren&#x2019;t there.&#x2019; He did what he had to do, but he was determined with getting on with the business of living,&#x201D; Scott says. &#x201C;He threw himself into &#x2018;Hamlet,&#x2019; and I threw myself into &#x2018;Elsinore.&#x2019; It was very important to me to not fetishize Ian&#x2019;s death, but to really think about his living. If everybody else was playing the tragedy around him, he was certainly looking toward the light and in some ways I tried to mirror that.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Meanwhile, you can also watch Scott talking about Charleson and the making of &#x201C;Elsinore&#x201D; with Oprah Winfrey on the latest episode of &#x201C;The Oprah Podcast.&#x201D;

SPOILER ALERT: This story discusses mild plot points for &#x201C; Hexed ,&#x201D; opening in theaters on Friday.

Walt Disney Animation Studios&#x2019; 65th film &#x201C;Hexed&#x201D; tells the story of the hidden world of witches and how, throughout history, they have been misunderstood. At its heart, however, is a story of motherhood and the powerful bond between a mother and daughter.

Disney animated films often kill off a parent to propel a story forward. But the creatives behind &#x201C;Hexed&#x201D; embraced that important relationship. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories ‘PAW Patrol’ Spinoff Series ‘Skye’s Pup Squad’ Set for 2027 Release

Directed by Fawn Veerasunthorn and Jason Hand, and co-directed by Josie Trinidad, the film follows Billie ( Hailee Steinfeld ), a rebellious teen who escapes into the secret world of Hexe, a realm of witches and wizards who live in harmony with nature.

Veerasunthorn explained that the story idea was originally pitched by Trinidad. &#x201C;She wanted to tell a story about the hidden world of witches. What if there&#x2019;s a place where they can thrive on their own? The place built by witches for witches.&#x201D; More importantly, Veerasunthorn notes, Trinidad wanted to tell a story of motherhood and the true heart of the story lies in the complicated, relatable relationship between Billie and her mother, Alice (Rashida Jones).

In developing Billie, she was portrayed as a modern teenager who wears combat boots and has an edgy style. Producer Yvett Merino explains that Billie oozes confidence: &#x201C;She doesn&#x2019;t quite fit in. There&#x2019;s something that feels different about her.&#x201D;

The key was making the film's main protagonist relatable. &#x201C;We all go through that at some point in our lives, especially in those teenage years where you're just trying to figure out who you are,&#x201D; Merino says. &#x201C;She takes her mom's car. She borrows her mom's car to go and free the school mascot. She's imperfect, impulsive and maybe doesn't always make the best decisions.&#x201D; Merino goes on to say, &#x201C;When I was a teenager, I didn't always make the best decisions. But you know what? I got away with it. We'll just learn from that lesson.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Imperfect relationships were key when it came to Alice as well. Alice is protective of Billie and wants to keep her daughter safe. Hand points out, &#x201C;We're all imperfect. We're all trying our hardest, but we're still figuring it out and that was really important to us.&#x201D;

Visually, the world of &#x201C;Hexed&#x201D; is vibrant and it took over 700 artists to bring it to life, sometimes with up to 40 people working on a sequence. &#x201C;The animation style pushed boundaries as far as they could by creating a world audiences had not seen before, filled with characters they&#x2019;d never seen,&#x201D; Veerasunthorn says.

The idea was that it would feel like a crisp autumn day after it had just rained and the air felt a bit chilly. &#x201C;It&#x2019;s a perfect place where magic can thrive,&#x201D; she adds.

Producer Roy Conli credits the film's production designer, Lorelay Bov&#xE9;, for her creativity. &#x201C;When people see this film, they will see a world they've never seen; they'll see characters they've never seen before in a Disney film.&#x201D;

If the textures of Hexe look heightened, that was a deliberate choice. &#x201C;We turn the dial up so it feels more like a caricature drawing could feel,&#x201D; Hand explains. &#x201C;We wanted this world to be so enticing to Billie. All of our decisions within the world of Hexe go back to Billie. When she goes out into that city for the first time, what&#x2019;s she going to want to see? Why is this world built for her? What is it speaking to her inside?&#x201D; Hand says. All those factors were important from both a production design standpoint, but also from a character standpoint. &#x201C;And then for that journey to bring her mom back into it, throws her for a loop. That&#x2019;s where the story starts to get its juice and interesting.&#x201D;

Voice casting was important too. Hand recalls seeing Steinfeld in &#x201C;True Grit&#x201D; and later in &#x201C;The Edge of Seventeen.&#x201D; In that film, Steinfeld plays a troubled teen who had a contentious relationship with their mom. He says, &#x201C;I always loved her in that role. I still loved her, even though she was doing the worst things and saying terrible stuff and that&#x2019;s a really great quality.&#x201D; But it was her voice quality that made her perfect to lead &#x201C;Hexed.&#x201D; &#x201C;Our animators even picked up on particular mannerisms of the way she holds her mouth, little micro expressions that she does.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Jones was perfect for Alice. Verasunthorn says, &#x201C;Rashida brings this sense of comedy in a very uptight mom. Those two words don&#x2019;t go well together, but somehow she makes it work. The depth of vulnerability that we get to see in Alice is quite beautiful.&#x201D;

&#x201C;Hexed&#x201D; wouldn&#x2019;t be a Disney movie without a villain to stir up a little trouble. Enter Jodie Foster, who voices Queen Celeste, a sinister ruler who stops at nothing to maintain her power.

Was it easy to get her to say yes? Conli says, &#x201C;We asked her and she did it. She&#x2019;d never played a villain before. She&#x2019;s done a phenomenal job at this incredible narcissistic witch that is a little over the top.&#x201D;

Joining Steinfeld, Jones and Foster are Walton Goggins as Beef Roger Krumchuk, a three-eyed cat.

&#x201C;He brought so much comedy and so much personality, way beyond what we ever imagined,&#x201D; Merino says.

As for the film&#x2019;s Easter eggs, there are plenty to look out for. Among them are Aladdin&#x2019;s magic carpet in Billie&#x2019;s bedroom, a floating head fortuneteller that nods to &#x201C;The Haunted Mansion.&#x201D; Mother Gothel from &#x201C;Tangled&#x201D; appears in a blink-and-you&#x2019;ll-miss-it moment.

Hand&#x2019;s favorite one is Cursula, a nod to &#x201C;The Little Mermaid&#x2019;s&#x201D; Ursula. &#x201C;It&#x2019;s voiced by Jodi Benson &#x2014; who provided the voice of Ariel in the original animated film. I love &#x2018;The Little Mermaid&#x2019; so much, and so to have Jodi Benson come in and do a complete twist on it and have her play Cursula, she was so amazing. She gave us such energy.&#x201D;

Merino and Conli concur that the scene with dancing brooms is one that is special for both of them. &#x201C;It reaches back to our history and goes back to Walt Disney&#x2019;s &#x201C;Fantasia,&#x201D; and the Sorcerer&#x2019;s Apprentice scene,&#x201D; Merino says.

&#x201C;The brooms, that's 80 years in the past. That's 'Fantasia'; it touches on this amazing legacy that we all live with, and we all celebrate.&#x201D;

For the biggest game the studio has ever released, Grand Theft Auto VI developer Rockstar Games wanted an equally ambitious soundtrack. Like much of the entertainment business these days, they turned to Atlantic Records to help make that happen.

Over the past decade, the record label&#x2019;s soundtrack efforts, spearheaded by Atlantic Music Group President Kevin Weaver, have established Atlantic as the de-facto landing spot for media companies looking to build a star-studded accompanying album for their work. Since 2015, Atlantic has handled the soundtracks for movies including Furious 7, Suicide Squad, Greatest Showman, F1, Twisters and most-famously Barbie, the latter of which became a cultural phenomenon alongside the film itself.

But the biggest opportunity Atlantic has seen to this point wasn&#x2019;t a movie, but rather a video game.

&#x201C;I went to Rockstar and said that they control the most culturally relevant IP on the planet, and that what they do with music is incredible,&#x201D; Weaver told The Hollywood Reporter over the phone from Miami &#x2014; where he&#x2019;d spent much of last week attending launch events for the game &#x2014; as he recalled the initial pitch to the company. &#x201C;Music is such an endemic part of the game and what GTA is. Why don&#x2019;t we endeavor to do something similar to what I&#x2019;d done on Barbie and these other soundtracks and A&R a whole lot of new records? &#x201D;

Weaver produced the soundtrack along with fellow Atlantic execs Joseph Khoury, Cody Verdecias, and Brandon Davis. GTA marked new territory for Weaver, the first time he&#x2019;d taken on a video game soundtrack, which as he acknowledges, wasn&#x2019;t on his purview before the game came into the fold.

&#x201C;I&#x2019;d never been interested in doing a video game soundtrack, to be honest with you,&#x201D; Weaver says. &#x201C;We license a lot of music to games, and I&#x2019;ve had plenty of game companies come to me over the years, but if I'm not moving the needle and elevating the next thing I do, I&#x2019;m not doing it. This was a natural choice, this was the one.&#x201D;

Similar to the process with film soundtracks, early on, Rockstar showed Atlantic some key scenes from the game they wanted music for that were mostly set to temp tracks to help show the overall tone and feel they were looking for.

Among the first artists they reached out to, Weaver says, was Travis Scott, with some of the other earlier asks including Morgan Wallen and Dua Lipa. Scott, Weaver says, turned in the first song, with &#x201C;Rhyno,&#x201D; one of the soundtrack&#x2019;s initial singles. Another Scott track, &#x201C;Burn This Shit Down,&#x201D; plays prominently during a key mission in chapter one.

The official soundtrack itself is just one aspect in the wider, rich musical world Rockstar has created for GTA VI. French electronic duo Justice, for example, provided the game&#x2019;s score. GTA&#x2019;s musical lifeblood, though, is the game&#x2019;s radio stations, which feature hundreds of songs across two dozen channels, hosted by real-life celebrities like Robyn, Wallen, Bad Bunny, Keith Richards and Lana Del Rey among many more. Atlantic didn&#x2019;t handle the radio stations, but Weaver says the company and Rockstar were &#x201C;attached at the hip,&#x201D; and some of those soundtrack offers came simultaneously with asks for the stars to host the radio shows.

Rockstar&#x2019;s vision wasn&#x2019;t set on any one genre, with the soundtrack spanning country, rock, hip-hop, blues, pop, electronic and latin among other genres. Just days into release, two of the game&#x2019;s needle drops have gone viral, with the game breathing new life into Carly Rae Jepsen&#x2019;s cult classic &#x201C;When the Lights Go Out&#x201D; and Dire Straits&#x2019; &#x201C;Money For Nothing.&#x201D; (Neither of those songs is on the official soundtrack, but they play in key missions in the game&#x2019;s first two chapters.) Jepsen has already re-released her song, hoping to build off the momentum and finally land it on the Hot 100.

&#x201C;Something Rockstar identified to us right away &#x2014; this isn&#x2019;t a rap game,&#x201D; Weaver says. &#x201C;It's not a country game or dance music game. All of this music lives within the game in so many different facets, and that gives us a great opportunity to go out and create records across pretty much every genre we want. It&#x2019;s GTA&#x2019;s taste and tone that makes this work.&#x201D;

The only real through-line, Weaver says, was capturing what he refers to as &#x201C;the glitz and grime&#x201D; of Vice City and Leonida, the game&#x2019;s stand-ins for Miami and the broader Florida area.

While Atlantic&#x2019;s more than used to handling a rollout for a film soundtrack, the strategy for video games is significantly different. While a movie&#x2019;s lifespan in the immediate zeitgeist is typically a few weeks &#x2014; pre-release marketing, the main theatrical window and post-theater streaming &#x2014; a video game like GTA will hold a captive audience for years. GTA V had a dedicated audience for 13 years before the latest game finally came out last week.

&#x201C;The tail on this never ends,&#x201D; Weaver says. &#x201C;Records are being discovered in the game in real time right now as the game is coming to market as it's come to market in the last 24 hours, so we kind of have an opportunity to see which records really start to raise their hand as well.&#x201D;

In the days since the game came out, Rockstar and Atlantic already surprise released a deluxe version of the soundtrack with 23 more songs atop the original 34, and today, they dropped four more songs from 100 gecs, Favored Nations, Joe Armon-Jones and Alex Frankel as iTunes exclusives.

As for any more musical plans going forward, Weaver says &#x201C;the world's just gonna have to wait and see.&#x201D;
